## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Breaking change for homepage UX**: The current homepage is a single-page app with client-side category switching, an emoji tray, and infinite scroll. The new architecture replaces this with a **Server Component** homepage that renders emoji grids as static HTML. Category switching will navigate to dedicated category pages (e.g., `/emoji/smileys-emotion`) instead of client-side filtering. The tray and copy-to-clipboard remain as client-side interactivity overlaid on top.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **`all-characters.json` will no longer be fetched for browsing**. It was 315 KB served to every visitor. Instead, each page will contain its own pre-rendered emoji as HTML buttons. The search index (`search-index.json`) will be a **separate, smaller file** (~80-90 KB) loaded **only** when the user interacts with search.

> [!WARNING]
> **Emoji detail pages**: The plan will statically generate pages for **all ~1,914 emojis** (not just the top 24). At build time this adds ~10-20 seconds but results in fully static SEO pages for every emoji. If you want to limit this to high-intent emojis only, let me know.

