## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Question 1**: Should the homepage remain a "picker" UI (category tabs + grid on one page) or become a landing/directory page that links out to category sub-pages? The architecture spec says category pages should be separate static routes. I'm proposing a **hybrid**: the homepage shows a featured grid of popular emojis (pre-rendered) plus links to category pages, while `/emoji/smileys-emotion`, `/emoji/animals-nature`, etc. are full category browse pages.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Question 2**: The current emoji detail page at `/emoji/[slug]` uses `dynamicParams = true` (default) which means un-pre-rendered slugs are built on-demand. Should we set `dynamicParams = false` so only pre-generated pages exist (returns 404 for invalid slugs), or keep ISR for any slug? I recommend `dynamicParams = false` since we'll pre-render all valid emojis.

